<title>MALAYSIA: Larut in China development project.</title>
<headline>Larut in China development project.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian property developer Larut Consolidated Bhd has entered into an agreement with Changchun City Urban and Rural Construction Committee to develop 124 hectares of land in China.</p>
<p>Larut said in a statement on Tuesday that the project in Changchun city, in Jilin province, would be a mixed development comprising residential and commercial units with a gross development value of about 3.3 billion renminbi.</p>
<p>The project, to be developed in several phases over five years, is expected to generate an estimated gross profit of 927 million renminbi, Larut said.</p>
<p>It said the project would be financed from internally generated funds and bank borrowings.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 8911)</p>
</text>
